<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nannuka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nannuka was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandela-dynasty">Chandela dynasty</a> in the early 9th century, ruling around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khajuraho">Khajuraho</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>, then called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jejakabhukti">Jejakabhukti</a>, probably as a feudatory of the Gurjara-Pratiharas. Chandela inscriptions name him as the first of the line, which became an independent power under his descendants Yashovarman and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhanga">Dhanga</a>.</p></div>
